, 1922. Oil on canvas, 8 x 7 inches. Private Collection. Private collection, Florida, 2024. © Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Materials description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/materials_description"}],"content":"Oil on canvas","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Measurement Description","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/measurement_description"}],"content":"8 x 7 inches","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"credit line","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300026687"}],"content":"Private collection, Florida, 2024","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"description statement","id":"https://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"}],"content":"A bright green apple, seen up close, sits on a partially visible black plate. The objects contrast with a plain white background.","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"provenance_narrative","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/provenance_narrative"}],"content":"(Alfred Stieglitz, New York, N.Y.) \nWilliam R. and Mary Emma Cooke Stockwell, New York, N.Y., 1923 \nWilliam R. Stockwell, Michigan City, Ind., 1929 \nEstate of William R. Stockwell, held by Ms. LaTourette Stockwell, Michigan City, Ind., 1961 \nConstance M. Baldwin, Milwaukee, Wisc., 1994 \nSotheby's, New York, N.Y., sale no. 6736, lot no. 189, 14 September 1995 \nPrivate Collection, 1995 \n(Alexandre Fine Art Inc., New York, N.Y.) \n(Source: Georgia O'Keeffe Museum, 2026)","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Holding Institution","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_instituion"}],"content":"Private Collection","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Copyright","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_copyright"}],"content":"© Georgia O'Keeffe Museum","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"Caption - Title and Date","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/caption_title_date"}],"content":"Untitled (Green Apple on Dark Plate), 1922","type":"LinguisticObject"},{"classified_as":[{"_label":"cr_remarks_1999","id":"https://data.okeeffemuseum.org/terms/local/cr_remarks_1999"}],"content":["Not recorded Whitney Archive, Downtown Gallery Archive, Abiquiú Notebooks. Stretcher inscription 1 dates 1922 and indicates no. 112 in 1923 New York (Anderson). Pictured in 1923 New York (Anderson) Stieglitz installation photograph, see Appendix III, figure 19. (Source: Lynes, 1999)"],"type":"LinguisticObject"}],"representation":[{"digitally_shown_by":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/713788/full/full/0/default.jpg","type":"DigitalObject"}],"classified_as":[{"_label":"Digital Image","id":"http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300215302","type":"Type"}],"digitally_available_via":[{"access_point":[{"id":"https://iiif.okeeffemuseum.org/image/iiif/2/713788"}],"conforms_to":[{"id":"http://iiif.io/api/image","type":"InformationObject"}],"format":"application/ld+json;profile='http://iiif.io/api/image/2/context.json'","type":"DigitalService"}],"type":"DigitalObject"}],"type":"VisualItem"}],"type":"HumanMadeObject"}